## Alternating Baguette Rings: $925 to $994

[![Baguette emerald cut diamond ring dot dash yellow gold alternating pattern](/images/baguette-emerald-cut-diamond-ring-dot-dash.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/site-search/jewelry?Diamonds=Dia,Lab&ComponentIDs=Ring&stoneShape=baguette&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

Alternating baguette rings mix baguette-cut and round brilliant diamonds in a repeating pattern. The visual result combines the step-cut discipline of the baguette with the sparkle of the round brilliant. This category leads all baguette ring styles in review count.

**Bar Setting Alternating Round and Baguette Cut Diamond Ring in 14k White Gold (JA) — [$925](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/bar-setting-alternating-round-and-baguette-cut-diamond-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315643?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

The lowest entry point in this lineup. Bar settings hold each stone between two parallel metal bars rather than in a channel wall. The bars lift each diamond slightly, allowing light entry from the sides.

The alternating baguette-round pattern in white gold is the cleanest execution of the mixed step-cut look at the lowest price available.

**Bar Setting Alternating Round and Baguette Cut Diamond Ring in 14k Yellow Gold (JA) — [$925](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/bar-setting-alternating-round-and-baguette-cut-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-315644?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

Same bar setting design in yellow gold. Yellow gold amplifies the warm tone of the baguettes — baguette cuts show color more readily than brilliant cuts, and yellow gold makes that warmth an intentional design element rather than a clarity concern.

**Dot Dash Diamond Ring in 14k Yellow Gold (1/4 ct. tw.) — [$994](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/dot-dash-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-1-4-ct-tw-item-194147?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (118 reviews)

The 118 Standard. Discounted from $1,420. The "dot" is the round brilliant, the "dash" is the baguette — alternating across 1/4 ct.

tw. of total diamond weight. 118 buyers validated this design at this price point, the highest review count in the baguette ring category.

**Dot Dash Diamond Ring in 14k White Gold (1/4 ct. tw.) — [$994](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/dot-dash-diamond-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-4-ct-tw-item-194149?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (118 reviews)

Same design in white gold. The white metal makes the baguette's flat top read as more colorless — white gold provides a neutral backdrop that doesn't add warmth to the stone's color, which matters in a channel-adjacent design where the baguette sits close to the metal.

**Dot Dash Diamond Ring in 14k Rose Gold (1/4 ct. tw.) — [$994](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/dot-dash-diamond-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-1-4-ct-tw-item-194148?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (118 reviews)

Rose gold version. The warmth of rose gold against the baguette's flat rectangular steps creates a visual depth that neither white nor yellow gold matches. The warm metal frame around a step-cut stone adds character.

The H-color baguettes in this setting look intentionally warm — not subpar.

