## Channel Set Baguette Bands: $1,640 to $3,290

[![Baguette emerald cut diamond ring channel set white gold wedding band](/images/baguette-emerald-cut-diamond-ring-channel-set.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/site-search/jewelry?Diamonds=Dia,Lab&ComponentIDs=Ring&stoneShape=baguette&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

Channel set baguette bands place pure baguette-cut diamonds in a continuous channel — no alternate stones, no pavé accents, no mixed cuts. The rectangular geometry of the baguette fills the channel with flat, parallel-line diamonds that look like a miniature architectural grid. This is the purest expression of the step-cut aesthetic in a band ring.

**Channel Set Baguette-Cut Diamond Ring in 14k Yellow Gold (1/2 ct. tw.) — [$1,640](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-baguette-cut-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-1-2-ct-tw-item-196124?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

The entry point for a full baguette channel band in yellow gold. Half-eternity coverage — baguettes across the top of the finger where they are visible. The 1/2 ct.

tw. weight means substantial coverage without maximizing cost. Works as a wedding band alongside an emerald cut engagement ring, extending the step-cut line across both rings.

**Channel Set Baguette-Cut Diamond Ring in 14k White Gold (1/2 ct. tw.) — [$1,640](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-baguette-cut-diamond-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-2-ct-tw-item-196123?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

Same design in white gold. White gold is the most popular pairing for a baguette band used alongside a white gold or platinum emerald cut engagement ring. The matching metal keeps both rings in the same visual register.

**Channel Set Baguette-Cut Diamond Ring in Platinum (1/2 ct. tw.) — [$2,190](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-baguette-cut-diamond-ring-in-platinum-1-2-ct-tw-item-196129?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

The same half-eternity baguette channel in platinum. Platinum's channel walls will hold baguette stones more securely than white gold over years of daily wear — the metal's density resists the micro-flexing that gradually loosens channel-set stones. For a wedding band worn daily alongside an engagement ring, platinum's durability advantage applies here as directly as it does for engagement ring settings.

[![Baguette emerald cut diamond ring pave crown designer band](/images/baguette-emerald-cut-diamond-ring-pave-crown.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/site-search/jewelry?Diamonds=Dia,Lab&ComponentIDs=Ring&stoneShape=baguette&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Channel Set Baguette Diamond Wedding Ring in 14k Yellow Gold — [$2,900](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-baguette-diamond-wedding-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-296637?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

Full eternity baguette band in yellow gold — baguettes run all the way around the finger, not just across the top. Full eternity means the step-cut grid is visible from every angle. This is the choice for maximum coverage and the most architectural baguette look available at this price tier.

**Channel Set Baguette Diamond Wedding Ring in 14k White Gold — [$2,900](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-baguette-diamond-wedding-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-296636?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

Same full eternity design in white gold. The most popular metal pairing for a baguette eternity band used as a wedding ring alongside an emerald cut engagement ring. White gold makes the baguettes the main visual event — the metal recedes, the stones lead.

**Channel Set Baguette Diamond Wedding Ring in Platinum — [$3,290](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/channel-set-baguette-diamond-wedding-ring-in-platinum-item-296641?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

Full eternity baguette in platinum. The highest durability option for full-coverage baguette coverage. Platinum's natural hardness means the channel walls maintain their grip on the rectangular baguette stones for decades without metal fatigue.

If the band will be stacked and worn daily against an engagement ring, platinum is worth the $390 premium over the white gold version.

