## Emerald Cut with Baguette Side Stones: The Classic Three-Stone

[![Baguette emerald cut diamond ring pave stack lifestyle hand close up](/images/baguette-emerald-cut-diamond-ring-pave-stack.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/site-search/jewelry?Diamonds=Dia,Lab&ComponentIDs=Ring&stoneShape=baguette&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

The classic three-stone emerald cut engagement ring with baguette side stones is the most direct interpretation of the baguette emerald cut diamond ring concept. One emerald cut center stone, two tapered baguettes on either side, set in a channel or prong configuration.

This design is associated with Harry Winston's classic three-stone style — the original tapered baguette flanking design that established the step-cut three-stone ring as the most architecturally coherent engagement ring format. The Winston approach uses trapezoid-cut side stones (a flat-top variant of the baguette with a tapered profile) that follow the emerald cut's rectangular outline precisely.

**Why tapered baguettes, not straight baguettes:**

Straight baguettes have parallel sides. Tapered baguettes narrow slightly toward the base, allowing them to follow the curved shoulder of the ring shank. The taper creates a natural transition from the side stone to the band — the geometry resolves without a visual gap.

Straight baguettes on either side of a center stone leave a visual break where the rectangular stone meets the curved shank.

**Stone sizing for 2ct and 3ct emerald cut rings with baguettes:**

A 2ct emerald cut (approximately 9mm × 6.5mm) needs side baguettes in the 0.25–0.35 ct each range to maintain proportion. A 3ct emerald cut (approximately 10.5mm × 7.5mm) needs 0.35–0.50 ct side baguettes each. The side stones should never exceed 60% of the center stone's length — if they match the center or come close, the eye loses focus on the main stone.

For [2ct emerald cut center stones](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.9&caratMax=2.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) or [3ct emerald cut center stones](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=2.9&caratMax=3.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), browse the certified inventory and match side stone sizing accordingly.

Lab emerald cut center stones are also an option — [browse lab IGI emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a 1ct+ lab center at a fraction of natural price.

